 "id": "2026-11-15-donbas-for-nato",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Give up the Donbas, get into NATO? Washington floated that trade. Kyiv's answer is complicated."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "That is Volodymyr Zelensky's account. He told reporters that U.S. negotiators asked whether Ukraine would leave the Donbas if it could join NATO. He says it is the first time membership was tied to land. Al Jazeera reports the areas in question are ones Russia does not control."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Zelensky says Ukraine will not hand over land, or recognise occupied areas as Russian. But with a full package, security guarantees, a strong army and money to rebuild, he would ask Ukrainians in a referendum. Guarantees like NATO's Article Five are his absolute minimum."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Washington has not confirmed the idea. Envoy Jared Kushner says only that several new ideas are being explored. No Kremlin reaction was reported, but Moscow has long rejected NATO membership for Ukraine."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Ukraine hold a referendum on the Donbas? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
