 "upload": {
  "title": "Zelensky: US Floated Donbas for NATO. Will Kyiv Bite? #shorts",
  "description": "Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky says U.S. negotiators raised the idea of Ukraine withdrawing from the eastern Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership. He spoke to reporters on Friday, November 13, 2026, after the U.S.-mediated trilateral talks with Russia in Abu Dhabi on November 10–11; his office released the remarks on Saturday. According to Zelensky, it was the first time NATO membership had been linked to territorial concessions. Al Jazeera reports that the parts of Donbas the U.S. asked about are areas Russia does not control. Zelensky said Ukraine would not give up territory and would not recognise occupied areas as Russian, but that with a comprehensive package — security guarantees, the right to a strong army, and funds for reconstruction — he would put the question to a national referendum. He called security guarantees modelled on NATO's Article 5 an \"absolute minimum\". The U.S. has not confirmed the proposal; envoy Jared Kushner said only that several new ideas emerged from the talks and are being explored, and that NATO will remain a critical pillar of European security. At the time of production, no Kremlin reaction to Zelensky's account had been reported; Moscow has long rejected NATO membership for Ukraine. The proposal is Zelensky's account and has not been independently confirmed.\n\nSources:\nCNN, Nov 14, 2026: US floated idea of Ukraine swapping land for NATO membership, Zelensky says\nNBC News / CNBC, Nov 14, 2026: U.S. floated idea of Ukraine ceding Donbas for NATO membership, Zelenskyy says\nAl Jazeera, Nov 14, 2026: US suggested Ukraine cede parts of Donbas to Russia to become part of NATO\nEuronews, Nov 14, 2026: US floats Ukraine ceding land to Russia in exchange for NATO membership: Zelenskyy\nABC News (Australia), Nov 15, 2026: US raised idea of NATO membership for Ukraine, Volodymyr Zelenskyy says\nRTÉ / France 24, Nov 14, 2026\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #NATO #Donbas",
